From ffbc496793836d288fd928cf86dcbeff04290bd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:21:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] DC8: GLASS and ADD 2D modes, prims in frame pixels,
 texture lookup by uid

The 2D layer gains what the house renderer needs:
- DC2D_GLASS: a palette texture times an ARGB, blended at its alpha (a
  translucent image); DC2D_ADD: a texture through the white bank times an
  ARGB, added at its alpha (a glow over an image's shape). pvr2d.c sets
  their PVR blends, swpvr.c renders them, an exact shade remaps a GLASS
  prim's texture like an image's, a palette lerp flags it.
- dc2d_tex_rect / dc2d_frect: textured and solid prims placed in frame
  pixels (the room's zoom scales them), dc2d_prim_count for counters.
- dc2d_tex_find: the slot of a resident texture by uid without its pixels,
  so a cached sprite needs no decode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
