From 43e05327864d5d5b67bb8da83678843d6564a879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:21:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] DC8: the dream house on the PVR (plat_room,
 dc/src/room.c)

plat_room and plat_room_project for the Dreamcast, portable C. It draws
exactly what core/src/room_ref.c draws (every wallpaper, floor, ceiling
ramp, roof, tint, room kind, fence and backdrop, the lamp pools, glow and
panes, the back facings, door and window skins, residents, cursor, rubber
band, pans), but:
- the static shell (roof, backdrop, walls, floor, lip) is rendered once
  with room_ref's pixel code into a PAL8 canvas and drawn as one texture
  until its key (size, view, origin, paints, patterns, light, lamps,
  backdrop, roof) changes; a pan only moves it;
- each piece is one sprite whose texture is keyed by everything its
  pixels depend on, in a table of keys with uids of their own; a resident
  texture is never decoded again;
- the order is room_ref's topological pick, found with Kahn's algorithm in
  O(n^2) instead of O(n^3) (dc_room_sort);
- ghosts and translucent residents are GLASS prims at 50%, the blueprint
  ghost a grey silhouette, an invalid ghost red, a selected piece an ADD
  glow that pulses; zoom 1 (a 1.6x close-up on the player) and 2 (Talk's
  framing) glide in and out, and plat_room_project follows them.
The mailbox gets the house's counters (room_us..room_prims_max; 4364 B)
and the harness commands 14 room-parity (a room_ref golden frame drawn by
plat_room on a screen of its own), 25 home-room and 26 money.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
