From 8488864d0a7715a1c7b85bb816999c55112ff17b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:21:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] DC8: host test of the house against room_ref
 (test_dc_room.c, the tee)

The dual-render host runner draws the house with room.c on the Dreamcast
side and room_ref on the native side (DC8_ROOM=ref: room_ref on both, the
route before DC8). dcroom_test (117 checks, part of make dc-host-test):
all 58 golden frames of core/tests/room_shells.h and every catalog piece
alone in 4 views and at night (1,745 frames) identical to room_ref pixel
for pixel through the software PVR; residents, tints, pans, the cursor and
the rubber band identical; squashes only inside their quads; the no-cache
boxes; the ghost, invalid, blueprint and selection effects; the order equal
to room_ref's search on 3,000 random layouts; the shell and sprite caches;
zoom 1 and 2 with plat_room_project; the busiest room's budget.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
