From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:21:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] DC8: make -C dc room-test, the house on Flycast

dc/tests/house/run_flycast.sh: the 58 room_ref golden frames drawn by the
game's own plat_room (dcrun room-parity, mailbox 14) against room_ref's
pictures at a 100% gate, and the house scripts (core/tests/scripts/
home_*.txt) tick-exact against the host software PVR (compare_house.py:
exact >= 99%, within 24/255 >= 99.9%) and reported against the native
runner; no prim dropped, no tick over 33.3 ms. dcrun learns the native
runner's home-room, money and up, and prints the house counters. The
target is the last step of the Flycast part of make -C dc test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
