Subject: [PATCH 6/9] DC5 audio-test: cut the stream's hold gaps before
 comparing envelopes

compare.py --drop-gaps N cuts runs of exact digital silence of N samples to
0.1 s after the first sound out of the Dreamcast WAV: the AICA stream's
gaps while the harness held the game at a sync stop, which are not the
game's sound. Whether a hold starves the stream depends on emulated
timing, so unrelated code can move a gap into the middle of a run: DC8's
build put a 1,001-sample gap into combat's WAV (the same sound, content
hash 0x664c5844 on both builds) and its envelope r fell from 0.920 to
0.859 against the single lag. run_flycast.sh passes --drop-gaps 256; on the
merge base it cuts nothing and changes no number, on DC8's build title
0.989, invasion 0.988, combat 0.904. Documented in DREAMCAST.md section 6.

